# PDF Processing & Chunking Rules

- Use `ingestPdf` (pdfjs-dist) to extract text; normalize whitespace.
- Detect chapters and titles during parse for metadata enrichment.
- Chunking: paragraph-level chunks plus a page-title chunk.
- Keep chunk sizes roughly 300–800 tokens where possible; later add sub-splitting if paragraphs are too long.
- Prefer deriving data (titles/chapters) over adding reactive state; keep business logic outside UI.
- For file outputs, use `saveExtractedPdf` for ranges and `splitPdfToPages` for per-page PDFs.
